# Azure DNS

## What It Is

Azure DNS hosts DNS zones and records using Microsoft infrastructure.

### Example

```text
contoso.com
```

Records inside the zone:

```text
www.contoso.com
mail.contoso.com
api.contoso.com
```

---

# Public DNS Zones

## Purpose

Resolve names from anywhere on the Internet.

### Example

```text
www.contoso.com
        ↓
20.40.50.60
```

A user anywhere can resolve the name.

---

## Common Record Types

### A Record

Maps hostname → IPv4 address.

```text
www.contoso.com
      ↓
20.40.50.60
```

### CNAME Record

Creates an alias.

```text
portal.contoso.com
          ↓
myapp.azurewebsites.net
```

### MX Record

Mail routing.

```text
contoso.com
      ↓
mail.contoso.com
```

### TXT Record

Commonly used for:

- Microsoft 365 Verification
- SPF
- DKIM
- Ownership Validation

---

# Private DNS Zones

## Purpose

Internal Azure-only name resolution.

### Example

```text
contoso.internal
```

Records:

```text
db01.contoso.internal
web01.contoso.internal
```

These names are NOT publicly accessible.

---

# Private DNS Zone Links

## Critical AZ-700 Concept

A Private DNS Zone must be linked to a VNet.

### Example

```text
Private DNS Zone

contoso.internal
        │
        │ Link
        ▼
     VNet-A
```

VMs in VNet-A can resolve:

```text
db01.contoso.internal
```

---

### Without A Link

```text
Private DNS Zone
        │
        X
        │
      VNet-B
```

Result:

```text
Name Resolution Fails
```

---

# VNet Peering vs DNS Links

## Common Exam Trap

Many students assume VNet Peering provides DNS resolution.

It does not.

### Example

```text
VNet-A
   ↔
VNet-B
```

Even if peering exists:

```text
VM-B
   ↓
app.contoso.internal
```

Still fails unless:

```text
Private DNS Zone
       ↓
Linked To
       ↓
VNet-B
```

---

## Memory Hook

```text
Peering = Connectivity

DNS Link = Name Resolution
```

You often need both.

---

# Auto Registration

Allows Azure VMs to automatically create DNS records.

Example:

```text
VM01
```

Automatically becomes:

```text
vm01.contoso.internal
```

---

# Exam Clue

Question mentions:

> "Automatically register private IP addresses"

Answer:

✅ Auto Registration

---

# Split-Brain DNS

## What It Is

Same domain exists in public and private DNS.

### Example

Public DNS

```text
app.contoso.com
      ↓
52.160.1.10
```

Private DNS

```text
app.contoso.com
      ↓
10.1.1.10
```

---

## Internal Users

Resolve:

```text
10.1.1.10
```

---

## External Users

Resolve:

```text
52.160.1.10
```

---

# Private Endpoints & DNS

## Common AZ-700 Topic

Private Endpoint:

```text
Storage Account
        ↓
Private Endpoint
        ↓
10.1.1.5
```

Applications access the service privately.

---

## DNS Requirement

Private Endpoints almost always require:

✅ Private DNS Zone

Without proper DNS:

```text
storageaccount.blob.core.windows.net
```

may resolve to the public endpoint.

---

